IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pa14-types`

-- Pensions Act 2014 (UK) — GOAL 3: BEREAVEMENT SUPPORT PAYMENT (ss 30-31).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-2014-19.txt.

§ `Goal 3 — bereavement support payment`

-- s 31(1) "the contribution condition is that, for at least one tax year
-- during the deceased's working life— (a) he or she actually paid Class 1 or
-- Class 2 national insurance contributions, and (b) those contributions give
-- rise to an earnings factor ... equal to or greater than 25 times the lower
-- earnings limit for the tax year." (3): treated as met for an employed
-- earner who died of an industrial injury or prescribed disease.
@ref s 31(1), (3)
GIVEN y IS A `Contribution year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the year meets the contribution test` y IF
        y's `actually paid Class 1 or Class 2 contributions`
    AND y's `earnings factor from those contributions` AT LEAST 25 TIMES y's `lower earnings limit`

@ref s 31
GIVEN b IS A `Bereavement facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contribution condition is met in` b IF
        any (GIVEN y YIELD `the year meets the contribution test` y) (b's `the deceased's contribution years`)
    OR  b's `died of an industrial injury or prescribed disease as an employed earner`

-- s 30(1) "A person is entitled to ... bereavement support payment if— (a)
-- the person's spouse, civil partner or cohabiting partner dies, (aa) in the
-- case of a person whose cohabiting partner dies, the person is pregnant or
-- entitled to child benefit in circumstances specified ..., (b) the person is
-- under pensionable age when [they die], (c) the person is ordinarily
-- resident in Great Britain, or a specified territory, ... and (d) the
-- contribution condition is met". (6): not for a death before the section
-- came fully into force. "Under pensionable age": the death is before the
-- day the claimant reaches it.
@ref ss 30(1), (6), 31
@export Whether a person is entitled to bereavement support payment under s 30 of the Pensions Act 2014 (UK): their spouse, civil partner or (if they are pregnant or entitled to child benefit as specified) cohabiting partner died while they were under pensionable age and ordinarily resident in Great Britain or a specified territory, the deceased met the contribution condition (s 31), and the death was not before s 30 came fully into force. Single claimant; the priority rules in s 30(1A)-(1D) are not applied. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN b IS A `Bereavement facts`  @desc The relationship, the death, the claimant's circumstances and pensionable age, and the deceased's contribution record
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is entitled to bereavement support payment` b IF
        relationshipQualifies
    AND b's `died on` LESS THAN b's `claimant reaches pensionable age on`
    AND b's `ordinarily resident in Great Britain or a specified territory`
    AND `the contribution condition is met in` b
    AND NOT (b's `death before section 30 fully in force`)
    WHERE
        relationshipQualifies MEANS
            CONSIDER b's `relationship to the deceased`
            WHEN `cohabiting partner` THEN b's `pregnant or entitled to child benefit as specified`
            OTHERWISE TRUE
